# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# INVESTIGATION NOTE: an EARLIER pair of CONTROL-A compiles (/tmp/ga3-ca-1, /tmp/ga3-ca-2), run immediately after
# this store finished its from-clean build and BEFORE this node's section_map-compaction fix, showed a divergence:
# every section's rendered content was byte-identical, but ONE of five queries' own EVIDENCE_OVERFLOW notice
# (CA-DEPS: 94 overflow items in both runs, but a different supplementary_packet_sha256) differed, cascading into
# a different manifest_sha256/packet_sha256/read_tokens. The divergence was investigated exhaustively before
# concluding it was NOT reproducible with the current code:
#   1. PYTHONHASHSEED hypothesis: REFUTED. Three concurrent compiles (PYTHONHASHSEED=0, PYTHONHASHSEED=0,
#      PYTHONHASHSEED=1) all produced the IDENTICAL packet_sha256/manifest_sha256
#      (f1bd438bea1911413a12d586d53ce73140a9aa05386481c771a0eaa66aef3941 /
#      f4d5e053b6fdba93dc2e5e28b03f8cde3ac5db7eaec94910b0059e0d5f70f813). A different hash seed did not reproduce
#      the divergence, and grep over govbridge/gather/{followup,engine}.py and config/facets.yaml found zero
#      wall-clock-budget code paths in this tree (the coordinator separately confirmed R1-GA2's pass-2, with a
#      wall budget, is not yet in this tree's base).
#   2. Drop-record comparison: the main packet's own per-item drop records (unit id + bytes + score + tier) were
#      100% IDENTICAL between the two original runs -- the SAME items, SAME byte counts, were dropped in both.
#   3. Semantic-route determinism: confirmed by the coordinator (deterministic embedding compute; fused/sorted by
#      (-score, id)).
#   4. Two further in-process compile_packet() calls (same Python process, same hash seed by construction): also
#      byte-identical.
#   5. This file's own seq1/seq2 pair (sequential CLI processes, mimicking the ORIGINAL divergent test's exact
#      methodology): byte-identical, PASS.
# Net: 6 of 6 clean re-runs with the current code match byte-for-byte; the divergence has not been reproduced.
#
# LEADING, UNCONFIRMED EXPLANATION (could not be proven directly): the coordinator's hypothesis that a TRANSIENT
# git read failure degraded one follow-up-resolved identifier to an honest MISSING in ONE of the two original
# runs (keeping the item COUNT the same -- exactly the observed symptom -- while changing its content/hash) is
# CONSISTENT with this tree's own code: govbridge/gather/followup.py's _safe_read_path/_safe_ls_tree_path
# (lines ~96-100, ~129-157) explicitly document degrading "a concurrent git gc/repack racing this read... observed
# directly: a `cat-file blob <oid>` failing with 'bad file' moments after `blob_at` resolved that same oid" to an
# honest MISSING rather than a crash -- exactly the shared, actively multi-agent repository this domain runs in
# (this session independently observed 2-3 sibling agents' own concurrent `index rebuild --from-clean` processes
# running AT THE SAME WALL-CLOCK TIME as the original divergent pair). CA-DEPS's own stop_reason
# (BUDGET_REACHED_WITH_UNRESOLVED after 1 followup round) confirms its follow-up identifier-resolution code path
# (where these safe-read wrappers live) WAS exercised. This mechanism could NOT be confirmed directly against the
# two original runs because `govbridge compile --out DIR` never persists a supplementary packet's own rendered
# content to disk (only its sha256 reaches the main manifest's EVIDENCE_OVERFLOW notice) -- a known, disclosed gap
# routed to R1-RA (see this node's checkpoint decisions/next_consumer) -- so the original divergent supplementary
# packets' own text could not be diffed after the fact.
# CONCLUSION: the compiler itself is deterministic (6/6 clean re-runs, including a same-methodology sequential
# replay, and a hash-seed cross-check that rules out Python-level nondeterminism). The one prior divergence is
# best explained by a disclosed ENVIRONMENTAL dependency already documented in R1-GA2's own code (transient git
# read failures under concurrent repository activity degrading a follow-up item to an honest MISSING), never
# reproduced with the current code, and outside this node's mutation_scope (govbridge/gather/**) to fix.

